  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Nazis stole an entire room, wall panels and all. Over six tonnes of carved amber, crated out of a palace near Leningrad in 1941.",
        "visual_query": "amber panels palace wall",
        "visual_fallback": "amber carving"
      },
      {
        "narration": "It took them thirty-six hours. The crates reached Koenigsberg that October and the room went back up inside the castle there.",
        "visual_query": "baltic port old town",
        "visual_fallback": "old harbour"
      },
      {
        "narration": "By early 1944 the panels were in boxes in the castle basement. Then the bombers came, and the city burned. Who moves a room during a siege?",
        "visual_query": "bombed german city ruins",
        "visual_fallback": "war ruins"
      },
      {
        "narration": "A Soviet investigator went looking in 1945 and found ash. Alexander Brusov reported the room was destroyed between the ninth and eleventh of April.",
        "visual_query": "burnt rubble ash ruins",
        "visual_fallback": "charred ruins"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Treasure hunters still dig for it anyway. A replica, twenty-four years in the making, opened at the Catherine Palace in 2003.",
        "visual_query": "gilded palace room interior",
        "visual_fallback": "gilded interior"
      }
    ],
